phaedo-opposites.logic.r3: argue/equivocates: P2 (S31): "opposites" is taken as contradictory states with nothing between (alive vs not alive), where nothing becomes "more dead" by degrees in P2 and as comparative or contrary opposites with degrees between them (greater/less, weaker/stronger), where a thing passes from one to the other by increase or decrease where opp is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C1 (S33) does not follow (phaedo-opposites.logic.r3.sense1)
phaedo-opposites.logic.r3: argue/countermodel: C1 (S33): D = {lifedeath}; genopp = ∅, opp = ∅, opp_2 = {lifedeath}, process = ∅
